the star-studded house of gucci is  inspired by the true story of italy's  infamous black widow who conspired to  murder her ex-husband but just how much  of the film is hollywood fiction versus  historical fact yapikai movie lovers i'm  jan and in this video i'm revealing the  biggest things that house of gucci got  wrong about the real story of patricia  reggiani and the gucci family the true  tale of patricia reggiani who came from  humble beginnings and married into the  rich and powerful guccis has plenty of  intrigue and drama however house of  gucci isn't shy about spicing things up  including patricia's wedding dress the  movie's costume designer prepared two  designs the first was modeled on the  real dress worn by patricia which  covered her all the way down to the  floor but director ridley scott opted  for an alternate design that was more  revealing and is a homage to famous  italian actress gina lola brigida  according to the film's costume cutter  even though the wedding scene was short  it was significant for the character so  the outfit had to have immediacy and  impact in the movie maurizio meets his  childhood friend paolo when he flees to  samaritans to get away from the italian  tax authorities the film plays up the  idea that his romance with paula began  while he was still with patrizia and  also that he decided to separate from  his wife while they were together in  switzerland in reality though the  details of maurizio's split with  patrizia were much different it happened  one weekend in 1985 when he told  patrizia he was going on a business trip  to florence left with a suitcase and  never came back it was left to a friend  to tell patrizia the next day that it  was actually over also in real life  maurizio didn't reunite with paula until  1990 a full five years after he left his  wife on top of that the movie completely  omits the fact that maurizio was  actually having an affair with a  different woman cherie mclachlan who  said their relationship spurred him on  to leave his unhappy marriage maurizio's  affair with mclaughlin lasted until he  met up with paula years later which did  happen in switzerland though it was  actually at a club and not on the ski  slopes i suspect the filmmakers omitted  the relationship with mclaughlin to  condense the story given the final films  already over two and a half hours long  and they chose to portray paolo over her  as that's who he's with at the time of  his death also having patrizia share  scenes with paolo ramps up the movie's  drama before the separation do you ever  steal anything paola i'm trying to teach  alessandra the importance of not  touching other people's belongings the  details surrounding habitrizia would  eventually have maurizio killed have  also been compressed and dramatized for  the movie in reality it appears patrizia  didn't meet with the people involved in  the murder as happens in the film  instead she asked lots of different  people if they'd help her then she got  her psychic friend pena to act as an  intermediary and find the assassins  there was also another person involved  who was the real getaway driver however  in the film his role has been merged  with one of the other conspirators also  in the movie the assassin shoots  maurizio three times twice in the back  and once in the chest but according to  the real-life concierge who witnessed  the murder the gunman shot maurizio a  total of four times three in the back  and a fourth time in his head this may  have been changed to make it a little  less gory in the movie and there's a  touch of extra drama in the trial with  patrizia refusing to answer to her  maiden name reggiani which in reality  she also did when signing her police  statement defiantly telling the judge to  call her senora gucci a reference to how  she continued to use the gucci name even  after her divorce and how she's  popularly known as lady gucci and like  lady gaga or lady gucci if you'd like  your own honorific title check out  established titles the sponsor of this  video established titles is a project  based on a historic scottish custom  where landowners are referred to as  leads or lords or ladies in english and  you can buy a piece of dedicated land in  scotland for as little as one square  foot which allows you to officially call  yourself a lord or lady so you can have  your own lady whistle down style title  in time for the next season of bridgeton  and with every order established titles  plants a tree to protect biodiversity in  scotland it's a new fun way to support  conservation and a great surprise gift  for your family and friends there are  even couple title packs available for  partners so you can get adjoining plots  of land you'll get an official  certificate with a crest proving your  title and a unique plot number on a  private estate in scotland you can use  your new title on credit cards plane  tickets even dating profiles plus you'll  be helping to preserve woodlands and  raise funds for charities like one tree  planted and trees for the future who  support global reforestation efforts  there's some amazing holiday deals on  title packs at the moment so visit  establishedtitles.comflix and use our  special code flicks to get an extra 10  off all purchases or tap the link in the  video description the filmmakers also  took some creative license when staging  maurizio's murder the movie's production  designer has said that the spot in milan  where the real murder took place was  draben and cinematic and they were  striving for a more heightened  atmosphere so he says they found a  section of rome with wide streets that  could credibly stand in for milan and  the area was a collage of architectural  styles gothic renaissance and arabic  that gave it a very operatic feel  the day maurizio was killed patrizia  famously wrote in her diary the single  word paradisos which in greek means  paradise in the movie however she writes  the italian version of the word paradiso  i imagine the filmmakers did this as  they thought it seemed more logical and  more people would quickly and easily  understand the italian word than the  greek one  the film team also opted for a much more  dramatic way to show how patrizia had  paola evicted from the home she'd been  sharing with maurizio in the movie  patricia turns up at the apartment and  after embracing paula tearfully orders  her to be shown out of what she now  calls her house i subscribe to  unconventional punishments back in the  real world this never happened instead  the eviction order was delivered via a  notarized letter drawn up around 11am on  the same day maurizio died just a few  hours after his death  although patrizia and maurizio's  daughter alessandra appears in the film  their second child allegra was  completely cut from the story i suspect  this was done to condense the already  long movie as even the daughter who does  appear isn't a crucial part of the  script also it means the filmmakers  could avoid casting more child actors  whose involvement in production brings  additional rules and regulations  especially as they'd already had to get  three actors to play alessandra over a  range of ages another interesting detail  absent from the final film is that after  patrizia was convicted her daughters  tried to get a retrial on the basis that  after their mother had an operation to  remove a brain tumour in 1992 she lacked  proper control over her mental faculties  at the time of the murder this did get  her sentence reduced by a few years  however since then both daughters seem  to more or less have cut ties with their  mother  when it comes to the look of the  characters although the movie's makeup  and hair team seem to have done a good  job with patrizia the real gucci family  have complained about some of the cast  claiming their depictions are  unflattering one of maurizio gucci's  cousins has said their grandfather aldo  was a lot taller than al pacino who  plays him and that pacino's overall  heavier look and sideburns compared  unfavorably to the real-life aldo who  she says was much more handsome plus she  also felt offended by jared leto's  untidy and fashionable look as paolo wow  you are gucci you need to dress the pot  after the release of the first trailer  some suggested lady gaga's accent was  more eastern european than italian and  since then francesca de martini an  italian actress who worked as a dialect  coach for salma hayek who plays pina  commented that while she was listening  to hayek's scene she thought gaga's  accent was a bit off sounding more  russian than italian i don't consider  myself to be a particularly ethical  person  but i am fair de martini also said there  are a lot of different accents in the  film with in her opinion al pacino  sounding more new york italian kochi is  what i say it is an adam driver's accent  being nearly non-existent as far as  fakes go they're pretty good at least  it's my name on the marks not yours and  then there's jared leto's paolo which  you can make your own mind up about  these are just mock-ups you picked the  real firecracker according to day  martino there wasn't a dialect coach on  set and she was only brought in at  hayek's request after the actress felt  she wasn't getting the accent quite  right don't let these forces around you  dictate who you are you are strong you  are magnificent now in lady gaga's  defense she revealed in an interview  with vogue that her method to get into  characters portraits here was very  intense she said she lived as her for a  year and a half and spoke with an accent  for nine months of that apparently never  breaking even off camera if you don't  know i'm gonna make sure you do she also  said it was impossible for her to speak  in the accent as a blonde so she  instantly dyed her hair and she added  that she worked hard on figuring out  patrizia's specific accent  and uses different ones depending on who  she's talking to in the film it's time  to take out the trash gaga began with a  dialect from vignola where patricia was  born and then moved on to what she  described as a higher class way of  speaking that would have been more  appropriate in places like milan and  florence whatever you think of the  accents though or credit goes to lady  gaga for improvising a line that's  already become iconic can you keep a  secret father son and house of gucci so  what do you think of house of gucci and  who gave the best and worst performances  let me know in the comments below if you  enjoyed this and a thumbs up and a share  are hugely appreciated and if you're a  fan of crime dramas tap left for my  latest you video with season 4 theories  about love's return or tap right for  something else you're sure to like  thanks for watching and see you next  time yippie kai movie lovers
 

